BUGS

This folder tracks the defects of this repository's project: one file
per bug.


NAMING

  B<n>-<short-name>.md, for example B1-focus-lost-after-unmap.md.
  Numbers count up from B1 and are never reused, even for a bug that is
  closed as a duplicate. Check the index below and the Git history
  before taking a number.


STATUS

  Reported      someone saw it; not yet reproduced
  Confirmed     reproduced, with steps written down
  In progress   someone is working on the fix
  Fix available the fix is in the source, but not yet checked in a build
                Fred runs
  Verified      the fix is checked in the build that ships it
  Deferred      real, but put off; say why and until when
  Closed        verified, or rejected or duplicate, with the reason

  Reopen a bug, under its own number, when the behaviour comes back.


SEVERITY

  Describes impact, not confidence or schedule.

  critical  crashes the program or session, loses work or data, or locks
            the user out
  high      breaks a core feature with no workaround
  medium    a feature misbehaves but a workaround exists
  low       cosmetic or rare

  IN THIS REPOSITORY, below, names the core features.


RECORD TEMPLATE

  Copy this into a new file:

    # B<n>: <title>

    - **Status:** Reported
    - **Severity:** medium
    - **Affected versions:** 0.0.1
    - **Fixed in:**
    - **Reported:** YYYY-MM-DD, by whom
    - **Found by:** R<n>, when a review found it

    ## What happens

    ## What should happen

    ## Steps to reproduce

    ## Cause

    ## Fix and verification

    Link the fixing commit, the regression test, and the exact build in
    which the fix was checked.

  Keep personal data, credentials and machine-specific logs out of these
  records. Describe a reproducer instead, and cite the system journal by
  boot and time window.


BUGS IN OTHER PROJECTS

  A bug found and fixed in a project we learn from (see ideas/) can
  teach us about our own code. Note it in that project's ideas file,
  with a link, and open a B record here only if our code has the same
  bug.


IN THIS REPOSITORY

  Core features: tam-file-select (desktop portal file chooser) and
  tam-journal (daily plain-text journal in Micro, with locking and
